ts: V9 migration test ✓\n- \"shared-tech/ accumulates domain imports over time\" → restructure-boundaries.test.ts: checker catches shared-tech→domain + the real-checker-subprocess test ✓\n\nSo all Flow 0 + Flow 6 TCs + the architecture-risk tests for Story 0 are covered. Good.\n\nBut wait — let me double-check the test-plan's \"Test Count Reconciliation\" for the Story 0 files:\n- restructure-boundaries.test.ts: estimated 8 tests. I wrote 11. ✓ (≥8)\n- assignment-config.test.ts: estimated 7 tests. I wrote 8. ✓ (≥7)\n\nGood — my test counts meet or exceed the estimates.\n\nNow, let me reconsider potential GAPS — obligations I might have missed:\n\n1. **The story's \"Production Path Proof\"** section says: \"Evidence: assignment-config.test.ts, restructure-boundaries.test.ts, and pnpm run boundaries.\" I have all three. ✓\n\n2. **The tech-design §Tech Arch Update** — I updated §System Shape. ✓\n\n3. **Anti-Shim Requirements** — all satisfied (no facades, no checker exclusions, no silent unknown keys). ✓\n\n4. **Transition-State Risk** — \"Existing old derivation rows are left in place and become unreadable\" (✓ — no proactive cleanup), \"Existing old queued work rows are deleted by a recorded thread-file migration with a warning\" (✓ — V9), \"New repair/rebuild/recovery writes the current derivation kind\" (✓ — all new code uses smooth_turn_compression).\n\nLet me reconsider a subtle one — the test-plan TC-0.4a says \"asserts schema DDL uses smooth_turn_compression\". My test asserts storage.ts contains smooth_turn_compression (the V5 backfill) and prompts/index.ts contains it. But does it assert the actual SCHEMA DDL? The schema DDL is the `derivation` table (TEXT derivation_type column — no CHECK constraint on the type value, so no DDL change needed for the rename). The \"schema DDL uses smooth_turn_compression\" really refers to the migration statements (V5 backfill INSERT). My test checks storage.ts contains smooth_turn_compression. That's the evidence. But is it 