{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202606190058064114fec49b5744fb","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.2","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The test enumeration confirms full TC coverage:\n\n**assignment-config.test.ts (8 tests):**\n- TC-0.3a ✓ (DERIVATION_TYPES not exported)\n- TC-0.3b ✓ (only inference assignments) + TC-6.3a ✓ (deterministic absent) — 2 tests\n- TC-6.1a ✓ (target ratios)\n- TC-6.2a ✓ — 3 tests (defaults, override, construction)\n- TC-6.4a ✓ (default lane/model)\n\n**restructure-boundaries.test.ts (11 tests):**\n- TC-0.1a ✓ (six domains top-level)\n- TC-0.2a ✓ — 2 tests (shared-tech exists, old folders gone)\n- TC-0.4a ✓ — 2 tests (smooth_turn_compression in schema/registry, no lower_band_projection except v9)\n- TC-0.6a ✓ (shared-tech→domain violation)\n- TC-0.6b ✓ (cross-domain internal violation)\n- + 2 allowed-direction tests + real-checker-subprocess\n- AC-0.4 architecture-risk ✓ (V9 migration deletes stale work + logs)\n\nEvery Story-0 TC (Flow 0: 0.1a, 0.2a, 0.3a, 0.3b, 0.4a, 0.5a, 0.6a, 0.6b; Flow 6: 6.1a, 6.2a, 6.3a, 6.4a) + both architecture-risk tests are covered by concrete tests. 19 new tests pass.\n\nTC-0.5a (verify-all green) — evidenced by the gate runs (all pass).\n\nSo pass 2 confirms: every obligation in the story/test-plan is either implemented (all TCs have tests) or explicitly surfaced (the 3 deferred items in findingsSurfaced + the 1 specDeviation). No missing evidence.\n\nLet me reconsider if there's anything ELSE in the test-plan or tech-design I haven't addressed for Story 0:\n\n- The test-plan's \"Golden cases for Deterministic Algorithms\" (concatenateDetailedChunk, classifyToolResult) — those are Story 2/5, NOT Story 0. Out of scope. ✓\n- The \"Manual Scenario Verification\" checklist — that's post-TDD-green manual verification with real models, Story 6+ territory. Out of scope for Story 0 implementation. ✓\n- inference-real.test.ts — Story 6. But I did update it (cast fix) so it still compiles/passes in CI-default posture. ✓\n\nSo Story 0's obligations are fully covered. No missing evidence.\n\nOne more consideration for pass 2 \"requirement alignment\": Let me double check the story's AC-6.2 more carefully. \"Defaults are installed for every derivation type; the defaults are used when the host does not supply explicit values.\" \n\nHmm — \"for EVERY derivation type.\" My DEFAULT_INFERENCE_ASSIGNMENTS covers the 4 INFERENCE types. The deterministic types (turn_rendering, chunk_summary_detailed) have NO default assignment (they're optional). Is that a gap vs \"every derivation type\"?\n\nRe-reading AC-6.3: \"Deterministic derivation types ... carry an assignment entry with provider and model optional; if present, they are not invoked during derivation.\" So deterministic types don't NEED defaults (they're optional and not invoked). AC-6.2's \"every derivation type\" — combined with AC-6.3 — means every type that NEEDS a default (inference types) gets one. The default assignment table in the tech design (§Default Assignment Table) lists the 4 inference types with defaults and the 2 deterministic as \"(deterministic)\" with no default lane/model. So my implementation matches the tech design's default table exactly. ✓\n\nAnd the guard defaults (AC-6.2's \"All guard values have defaults filled at construction\") — resolveGuards fills all guard values. ✓\n\nSo AC-6.2 is fully satisfied.\n\nLet me also reconsider AC-6.1: \"The model assignment config accepts optional per-derivation target range fields (min ratio, mid ratio, max ratio) and an optional input-size cap alongside provider/model/prompt.\"\n\nWait — \"an optional input-size cap alongside provider/model/prompt.\" Hmm. AC-6.1 mentions an \"input-size cap\" on the assignment. But the tech design (TDQ-7) puts the input-size cap (maxInferenceTokens) under DerivationGuards.smoothedPrompt, NOT on ModelAssignment. Let me re-read.\n\nAC-6.1: \"accepts optional per-derivation target range fields (min ratio, mid ratio, max ratio) and an optional input-size cap alongside provider/model/prompt.\"\n\nThe tech design TDQ-7 / ModelAssignment:\n```\ninterface ModelAssignment {\n  provider: string;\n  model: string;\n  prompt: string;\n  thinking?: ...;\n  targetMinRatio?: number;\n  targetMaxRatio?: number;\n  targetAimRatio?: number;\n}\n```\nNO input-size cap on ModelAssignment. The input-size cap is `guards.smoothedPrompt.maxInferenceTokens`. So AC-6.1's \"optional input-size cap alongside provider/model/prompt\" — the tech design RESOLVED this by putting the cap under guards (TDQ-7 issue #2: \"Split into typed per-derivation guard fields\"). So the design decision overrides the AC's literal wording — the cap is on guards, not the assignment.\n\nMy implementation: ModelAssignment has target ratios (no cap); guards.smoothedPrompt.maxInferenceTokens is the cap. This matches the tech design (TDQ-7), which is the authoritative resolution. The story's AC-6.1 wording is pre-resolution; the tech design resolved it. So my implementation aligns with the RESOLVED design. ✓\n\nAnd TC-6.1a (test-plan): \"construction with targetMinRatio/targetMaxRatio/targetAimRatio on an assignment → accepted.\" My test covers target ratios accepted. The cap is tested via TC-6.2a (guard defaults). ✓\n\nSo AC-6.1 is satisfied per the design resolution. Good.\n\nOK — pass 2 is thorough. Every obligation is implemented or surfaced. No new findings to fix. The implementation is complete and correct.\n\nLet me reconsider whether I should make ANY change for pass 2. The review found no new defects — coverage is complete, alignment is correct (including the AC-6.1 cap-on-guards resolution). So no code changes needed for pass 2. I'll re-emit the JSON, possibly adding a note that pass 2 confirmed coverage. But the output contract doesn't have a \"pass number\" field. I'll just re-emit the same payload (it's accurate), perhaps with a small refinement to planSummary or findingsSurfaced noting pass-2 confirmation.\n\nActually — since pass 2 found no new fixes, the payload is essentially unchanged from after pass 1. The gates are still green. Let me re-emit the payload. I could add a finding to findingsFixed noting \"pass 2 confirmed full TC coverage\" but that's not a \"fix.\" Let me keep findings accurate — pass 2 was verification, found nothing to fix. I'll keep the payload as-is (it already reflects the final state after pass 1's comment fix), since pass 2 made no changes.\n\nWait — but I should be careful: the instructions say \"Do not skip required fixes, open questions, or surfaced risks.\" Pass 2 found no required fixes. So I re-emit. Let me make sure the payload is the final accurate one.\n\nThe payload from after pass 1 is accurate and current. Let me re-emit it (the gates are green, 452 tests, all TCs covered). I'll keep it substantively the same since pass 2 required no changes. I might tweak planSummary to note pass-2 coverage confirmation, but that's cosmetic. Let me re-emit the final payload cleanly.\n\nActually, let me reconsider one thing about evidence for TC-6.4a. My test calls `sdk.config.provider.smoothPrompt(...)` etc. and checks `log[0].provider === \"codex\"`. This proves the default assignment's provider lane is used. Good evidence. But let me double-check the test actually exercises all 4 inference types and asserts each. The INFERENCE_OPS has 4 entries (smoothed_prompt, tool_result_summary, smooth_turn_compression, chunk_summary_brief), and the test iterates all 4, then asserts ALL log entries have provider codex + model gpt-5.4-mini. So all 4 inference types' defaults are verified. ✓ Strong evidence.\n\nEverything checks out. Re-emitting the final payload.\n\nLet me reconsider the gatesRun — should I re-list them? I ran verify, green-verify, verify-all all pass. The last green-verify (after pass 1 fixes) was green. Pass 2 made no changes, so the gates are still green. I'll list them as pass.\n\nFinal payload — same as after pass 1, since pass 2 found nothing to fix. Let me re-emit it.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d429f632-d6b9-4c8a-a0e2-2802260578d5","uuid":"bebe6fdf-ab46-4a0e-b5da-dc45a453d161"}
