g inference types — rewrote to validate against DEFAULT_INFERENCE_ASSIGNMENTS keys and fill defaults (AC-6.2/6.4).\",\n      \"Extract<string, literal-union> evaluated to never after DerivationType→string in chunk-recovery — replaced with the explicit literal union.\",\n      \"record-red-manifest had captured red-manifest.json's own hash, making it self-stale — removed the self-entry.\",\n      \"Self-review pass 1: two src comments still read 'shared/ may not import domains/' after the restructure — corrected in context.ts and derivation.ts.\",\n      \"Self-review pass 2: verified every Story-0 TC (0.1a/0.2a/0.3a/0.3b/0.4a/0.5a/0.6a/0.6b/6.1a/6.2a/6.3a/6.4a) maps to a named passing test and both architecture-risk tests have coverage; no missing evidence, no further fixes.\"\n    ],\n    \"findingsSurfaced\": [\n      \"Prompt file lower-band-v1.ts is intentionally NOT renamed to smooth-turn-compression-v1.ts: the registry KEY was renamed (smooth_turn_compression), but the tested prompt content is Story 3's deliverable (AC-1.2), so renaming the file now would mislabel placeholder content. AC-0.4 is satisfied via the type-string rename (TC-0.4a passes).\",\n      \"Deterministic prompt files turn-compose-v1 and chunk-detailed-v1 remain in the prompt registry — their removal is coupled with removing composeTurnRendering/summarizeChunkDetailed from the DerivationProvider interface, which is Story 3/4 scope (the handlers still route them through the provider in Story 0).\",\n      \"The deterministic provider output marker stays \\\"projection\\\" while the method was renamed compressSmoothTurn; the marker is internal test-double text that no AC covers and that inference-adapter/fixtures tests pin.\",\n      \"AC-6.3's 'deterministic types are not invoked during derivation' is the Story 3/4 end state: in Story 0 the handlers still call composeTurnRendering/summarizeChunkDetailed through the provider, so Story 0 realizes only the construction-acceptance half (deterministic assignments optional), which TC-6.3a covers.\",\n      \"AC-6.1's 'input-size cap alongside provider/model/prompt' is resolved by tech-design TDQ-7 to live on DerivationGuards.smoothedPrompt.maxInferenceTokens rather than on ModelAssignment; implementation follows the resolved design and TC-6.1a/TC-6.2a cover both the target ratios (assignment) and the cap (guards).\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"openQuestions\": [],\n  \"specDeviations\": [\n    \"Prompt module lower-band-v1.ts not renamed to smooth-turn-compression-v1.ts (only the registry key and derivation-type string were renamed). Deferred to Story 3, which installs the tested prompt content and can rename the module then. TC-0.4a (schema/source use smooth_turn_compression, no derivation-type references under the old name) passes.\"\n  ],\n  \"recommendedNextStep\": \"Proceed to verification, then Story 1 (Smoothed-prompt guards). The foundation — flat domain layout, shared-tech consolidation, smooth_turn_compression type, default assignments, guard defaults, enforced boundaries, and the stale-work migration — is in place for Stories 1–5.\"\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d429f632-d6b9-4c8a-a0e2-2802260578d5","total_cost_usd":0.535887,"usage":{"input_tokens":7314,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":619584,"output_tokens":7581,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"glm-5.2[1m]":{"inputTokens":7314,"outputTokens":7581,"cacheReadInputTokens":619584,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.535887,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"803dc32e-b220-4604-8b09-2d43fcca039f"}
