. threadsDomain is the scoped surface? No — `threadsDomain` is the raw module import (`import * as threadsDomain from \"./threads/index.js\"`), and `drainDeps.openThreadDatabase = threadsDomain.openThreadDatabase` (the raw function, NOT scoped). Good — the scheduler gets the raw opener (which runs migrations). The scheduler calls `deps.openThreadDatabase(filePath)` → returns OpResult<DatabaseSync>. ✓. This matches ThreadDbOpener = (path) => OpResult<DatabaseSync>. ✓. Production path: background drain opens thread DB via the injected opener → migrations run → drain proceeds. ✓.\n\nLet me verify this is actually wired correctly by checking sdk.ts line ~506 (drainDeps.openThreadDatabase = threadsDomain.openThreadDatabase). I set that earlier — it was already there from the prior pass. And ThreadDbOpener type now matches. ✓.\n\nOK let me do the concrete TODO grep and then conclude. Let me also re-confirm the full verify one final time since this is the handoff (pass 3 = \"fix before handoff\"). Actually, I haven't changed anything since pass 2 (pass 2 found nothing). So the gates are still green from the pass-1 green-verify run. But to be rigorous for handoff, let me re-run verify-all (the epic gate) once more as the final confirmation, and grep for TODOs.\n\nLet me run: grep TODO/FIXME in src + verify-all.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d429f632-d6b9-4c8a-a0e2-2802260578d5","uuid":"e0df6838-20af-4b93-aec4-5cb044a5de40"}
